verses.text:
“I will sweep away man and beast;
I will sweep away the birds of the heavens
and the fish of the sea,
and the stumbling blocks along with the wicked.{b}
I will cut off mankind
from upon the face of the ground,” declares Yahweh.

“I will stretch out my hand against Judah
and against all the inhabitants of Jerusalem;
and I will cut off from this place the remnant of Baal,
and the name of the idol priests along with the priests;{c}

those who bow down on the rooftops
to the host of the heavens;
those who bow down and swear to Yahweh
and yet swear by Malcam;{d}

Be silent before the Lord Yahweh!
For the day of Yahweh is near;
Yahweh has prepared a sacrifice;
he has consecrated his guests.

Howl, you who dwell in the Mortar!{g}
For all the people of Canaan are brought to silence;
all who weigh out silver are cut off.

Seek Yahweh, all you humble of the land,
who do his justice;
seek righteousness; seek humility;
perhaps you will be hidden
on the day of the anger of Yahweh.{b}

For Gaza shall be forsaken,
and Ashkelon a desolation;
Ashdod they shall drive out at noon,
and Ekron shall be uprooted.{c}

Woe to the inhabitants of the seacoast,
the nation of the Cherethites!{d}
The word of Yahweh is against you,
O Canaan, land of the Philistines;
and I will destroy you until no inhabitant is left.

The coast shall belong to the remnant of the house of Judah;
on it they shall graze;
in the houses of Ashkelon
they shall lie down at evening.
For Yahweh their God will visit them
and restore their fortunes.

Herds shall lie down in her midst,
all the beasts of every nation;{i}
both the desert owl and the hedgehog
shall lodge among her column tops;
a voice shall sing in the window;
desolation shall be on the threshold;
for he has laid bare the cedar work.

She has not listened to the voice;
she has not accepted correction.
She has not trusted in Yahweh;
she has not drawn near to her God.

Her officials within her are roaring lions;
her judges are wolves of the evening
that leave nothing until the morning.

Her prophets are reckless,
men of treachery;
her priests have profaned what is holy;
they have done violence to the law.

Yahweh within her is righteous;
he does no injustice;
morning by morning he brings his justice to light;
he does not fail;
but the unjust knows no shame.

“I have cut off nations;
their corner towers are desolate;
I have laid waste their streets
so that no one passes along them;
their cities are laid waste,
without a man, without an inhabitant.

“For then I will turn to the peoples a purified lip,{c}
that they may all call upon Yahweh’s name
and serve him with one shoulder.{d}

From beyond the rivers of Cush
my worshipers, the daughter of my scattered ones,
shall bring my offering.{e}

The remnant of Israel shall do no injustice
and speak no lies,
nor shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth;
for they shall graze and lie down,
and none shall make them afraid.”

Yahweh has removed your judgments;
he has turned back your enemy.
The King of Israel, Yahweh, is in your midst;
you shall never again fear evil.

On that day it shall be said to Jerusalem:
“Do not fear, O Zion;
let not your hands grow weak.

Yahweh your God is in your midst,
a mighty one who will save;
he will rejoice over you with gladness;
he will be quiet in his love;{f}
he will exult over you with loud singing.”

“I will gather those who grieve for the appointed feasts;
they were from you,
a burden of reproach upon her.{g}
